= Proof — Technical =

== Formal derivation ==
Given axioms Γ and a proof calculus:

<pre>
Γ ⊢ φ
</pre>

means there exists a finite derivation of φ from Γ under the system's rules.

== Proof systems ==
Common proof formalisms include:

* natural deduction;
* sequent calculus;
* Hilbert systems;
* tableaux;
* resolution;
* type-theoretic proof terms.

Different systems can prove the same theorems while exposing different structural properties.

== Proof theory ==
Proof theory studies derivations as mathematical objects.

Topics include normalization, cut elimination, consistency, ordinal analysis, and proof complexity.

== Formalization gap ==
Ordinary mathematical proofs compress many steps.

Formal proof assistants require these gaps to be reconstructed using explicit definitions and libraries.

This can reveal hidden assumptions without implying informal mathematics is invalid.

